{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Choose for us men.</b> Amalek was great in the wisdom of astrology and chose the men of his army to be men who could not die in that year, for he knew this through the wisdom of the stars and the constellations. Therefore Moses said to Joshua, ״בחר לנו אנשים״ — choose for us men like them, so that he would not be able to outwit us by killing men of Israel while Israel would not kill a single one of them. And this is what is written: ״ויחלש יהושע״ — and Joshua weakened — and it does not say 'and he killed.' And the fact that he said ״בחר לנו״ — 'choose for us' — putting him on equal footing with himself, instead of saying 'choose for me,' the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: from here, let the honor of your student be as dear to you as your own."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:27.611601765Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}